<section id="key-takeaways" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="key-takeaways">Key Takeaways</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong><code>requires_grad=True</code></strong> tells PyTorch to record operations for differentiation.</li>
<li><strong><code>.backward()</code></strong> traverses the computational graph in reverse, applying the chain rule.</li>
<li><strong>Gradients accumulate</strong> — always call <code>.zero_()</code> before the next backward pass.</li>
<li><strong><code>torch.no_grad()</code></strong> and <strong><code>.detach()</code></strong> let you opt out of tracking when you don’t need gradients.</li>
</ul>


